  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e93ca21b-3de7-4822-9eea-336fa561f158-image12.png\" /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/191d9a06-dc45-4553-be0f-0a7619122dc3-image13.png\" /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/36318772-69a0-4a67-8988-090481baab3d-image14.png\" /></p><p>The equivalent resistance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;of this given network is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>90</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>160</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>By applying ohm&#39;s law, the Current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi></math>&nbsp;through the battery is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mfrac><mn>160</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>160</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>9</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p>",
